/**
@defgroup log log: logging
@brief Named spdlog loggers sharing one configuration, and log throttling.

Every component fetches its own logger once (`log::get("db.pool")`) and keeps
it. Logger names are dotted by module, so levels can be tuned per area in the
configuration (`"levels": {"db.sql": "trace"}`). LogThrottle keeps a failure
loop from flooding the log.

Library: `caelitus::log`. Depends on: spdlog.

@defgroup core core: dates, time zones, errors
@brief Small building blocks used by every other module.

- Timestamp, Date and the ISO 8601 / RFC 3339 conversions;
- TimeZone, which knows the EU daylight saving rule;
- the domain error hierarchy (DomainError and its subclasses) that services
  throw and the API layer maps to JSON-RPC errors.

Library: `caelitus::core`. Depends on: @ref log.

@defgroup json json: JSON conversions
@brief nlohmann::json conversions for the core types (Timestamp, Date, std::optional).

Header-only. Library: `caelitus::json`. Depends on: @ref core, nlohmann/json.

@defgroup cache cache: in-memory cache
@brief A thread-safe, read-optimized key/value cache.

cache::LocalCache serves lookups in parallel under a shared lock and lets
writers in ahead of new readers (cache::WriterPreferringMutex). It has no
expiry or size bound: its owner decides what is in it (see catalog::BookCache).

Header-only. Library: `caelitus::cache`.

@defgroup scheduler scheduler: periodic jobs
@brief Named jobs on schedules ("every 15s", "rate 1s", cron), with status, pause/resume and manual runs.

scheduler::Scheduler runs jobs on one timer thread and a small worker pool; a
job never overlaps itself. scheduler::Schedule parses the schedule texts used
in the configuration, and scheduler::CronExpression evaluates cron expressions
in a local time zone, across summer-time changes. Knows nothing about the
catalog: the application defines its jobs in app::Application, and the API
exposes them as scheduler.* methods.

Library: `caelitus::scheduler`. Depends on: @ref core, @ref log.

@defgroup db db: database access
@brief Database access that knows no particular database.

The layers, from the services down:

| Layer                 | Type                                   | Role |
|-----------------------|----------------------------------------|------|
| transactions          | db::ITransactionManager, db::TransactionManager | Groups statements of one use case; retries deadlocks |
| statements            | db::SqlExecutor                        | Runs one statement on the current transaction's connection, or on a pooled one |
| connections           | db::ConnectionPool                     | Reuses connections, validates them, limits their number |
| driver                | db::IConnection, db::IConnectionFactory | The only thing that knows the database product (see @ref db_mariadb) |

Errors are translated into the db::DatabaseError hierarchy, so callers never
see driver exceptions. db::MigrationRunner applies versioned schema changes.

Library: `caelitus::db`. Depends on: @ref core, @ref log.

@defgroup db_mariadb db_mariadb: MariaDB driver
@brief db::IConnection implemented on MariaDB Connector/C++.

The only code that includes the connector's headers; it also maps MariaDB
error numbers to the db::DatabaseError hierarchy.

Library: `caelitus::db_mariadb`. Depends on: @ref db, MariaDB Connector/C++.

@defgroup mqtt mqtt: MQTT client
@brief Library-independent MQTT client: interfaces, subscriptions, reconnects, last will.

Services only see mqtt::IMqttPublisher. mqtt::MqttClientBase implements
everything that does not depend on the client library (subscription registry,
handler dispatch on a dedicated thread, online/offline status, statistics,
throttled logging); see @ref mqtt_mosquitto for the transport.

Library: `caelitus::mqtt`. Depends on: @ref log.

@defgroup mqtt_mosquitto mqtt_mosquitto: libmosquitto transport
@brief mqtt::MosquittoClient, the MQTT client on libmosquitto.

Library: `caelitus::mqtt_mosquitto`. Depends on: @ref mqtt, libmosquitto.

@defgroup net net: TCP server
@brief Asynchronous TCP server for `\0`-terminated request/response messages (Asio).

net::TcpServer accepts connections, splits the byte stream at `\0` bytes and
hands each message to a net::IMessageHandler on a worker pool, answering in
order per connection. It knows nothing about JSON-RPC.

Library: `caelitus::net`. Depends on: @ref log, Asio.

@defgroup catalog catalog: book catalog domain and services
@brief The business logic: books, authors, categories, reviews, likes.

- **domain**: plain data (Book, Author, ...), typed ids, validation rules and
  the repository interfaces the services need;
- **services**: one class per aggregate (BookService, ReactionService, ...).
  They validate input, enforce the rules, group work in transactions and
  publish events; they know neither the database nor the MQTT library.

Library: `caelitus::catalog`. Depends on: @ref core, @ref cache, and the
interfaces of @ref db and @ref mqtt.

@defgroup catalog_mariadb catalog_mariadb: catalog repositories on MariaDB
@brief The catalog's repository interfaces implemented in SQL, and its schema migrations.

Library: `caelitus::catalog_mariadb`. Depends on: @ref catalog, @ref db.

@defgroup api api: JSON-RPC API
@brief JSON-RPC 2.0 protocol handling, the catalog methods, OpenRPC and the MQTT like listener.

- api::JsonRpcHandler parses requests, validates parameters against each
  method's JSON Schema, runs the method and maps exceptions to error codes;
- api::registerCatalogApi() declares every catalog method;
- api::openRpcDocument() describes them as an OpenRPC document;
- api::MqttReactionListener turns MQTT like/dislike messages into calls to
  catalog::ReactionService;
- api::registerOperationsApi() exposes the scheduled jobs (scheduler.*) and the
  health report (system.health).

Library: `caelitus::api`. Depends on: @ref catalog, @ref json, @ref net, @ref mqtt, @ref scheduler.

@defgroup config config: configuration
@brief Loads and validates `config.json`, with `${ENV_VAR}` substitution.

Library: `caelitus::config`. Depends on: @ref db, @ref mqtt, @ref net, @ref log, @ref json.

@defgroup app app: the server
@brief `main()`; app::Application, which creates, wires, starts and stops every
component and defines the scheduled jobs; app::HealthMonitor, the "health" job.

Library: `caelitus::app` (so the end-to-end tests can run the real server), plus
the `caelitus` executable (`main.cpp`).
*/

/// @namespace caelitus
/// Everything in this project.

/// @namespace caelitus::log
/// Logging; see @ref log.

/// @namespace caelitus::db
/// Database access; see @ref db.

/// @namespace caelitus::db::mariadb
/// The MariaDB driver; see @ref db_mariadb.

/// @namespace caelitus::mqtt
/// MQTT client; see @ref mqtt.

/// @namespace caelitus::net
/// TCP server; see @ref net.

/// @namespace caelitus::catalog
/// Book catalog domain and services; see @ref catalog.

/// @namespace caelitus::catalog::rules
/// Validation and normalization rules for catalog input.

/// @namespace caelitus::catalog::mariadb
/// Catalog repositories on MariaDB; see @ref catalog_mariadb.

/// @namespace caelitus::api
/// JSON-RPC API; see @ref api.

/// @namespace caelitus::scheduler
/// Periodic jobs; see @ref scheduler.

/// @namespace caelitus::app
/// The server executable; see @ref app.

/// @namespace caelitus::cache
/// In-memory cache; see @ref cache.

/// @namespace caelitus::api::schema
/// Builders for the JSON Schemas that describe API parameters and results.
